data.content:
Here are the improved MSTest 3.x+ collection assertions:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetActiveUsers_ReturnsOnlyActiveUsers()
{
    var service = new UserService();
    var users = service.GetActiveUsers();

    Assert.IsNotNull(users);
    CollectionAssert.HasCount(users, 3);
    Assert.IsTrue(users.All(u => u.IsActive));  // no collection shortcut for predicate-all
    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<User>(
        users.Single(u => u.Role == "Admin"));
}
```

**Key replacements:**

| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `Assert.IsTrue(list.Count > 0)` | `CollectionAssert.IsNotEmpty(list)` |
| `Assert.IsTrue(list.Count == 3)` | `CollectionAssert.HasCount(list, 3)` |
| `Assert.IsTrue(x != null)` | `Assert.IsNotNull(x)` or `Assert.IsInstanceOfType<T>(x)` |
| `Assert.IsTrue(list.Contains(x))` | `CollectionAssert.Contains(list, x)` |
| `Assert.IsTrue(!list.Any())` | `CollectionAssert.IsEmpty(list)` |

These give **much better failure messages** — e.g. `HasCount` reports "Expected 3 but found 5" instead of just "Assert.IsTrue failed".
